  "query_preview": "models and their ensemble counterparts are showing a\nsecond large upper level trof moving across the western United\nStates Sunday. This UL feature should move across Kansas during\nthe Monday afternoon to early Tuesday morning period. It should\nbe noted that several ensemble members are indicating the\npassage of an open and progressive upper level wave. There has\nbeen a noted trend in keeping this wave open and not closed and\ndeep anymore. If this continues to hold true, rainfall amounts \nand winds would be less impressive than compared to a previously\nadvertised deep and closed system. Regardless, unsettled \nweather looks on track for Monday and Tuesday. Beyond that, the \nensembles are in better agreement with an upper level ridge to \nprevail with a drier and warmer forecast as a result.",
